# Phase G1 evidence is byte-compared and generated with deterministic LF.
/.gitattributes text eol=lf
/build.gradle text eol=lf
/src/g1tool/**/*.java text eol=lf
/tools/g1_benchmark_gate.py text eol=lf
/tools/g1_model_proofs.json text eol=lf
/tools/g1_performance_benchmark.json text eol=lf
/tools/g1_render_parity.py text eol=lf
/tools/layer_definition_to_geo.py text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/g1_proof/**/*.json text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/g1_proof/**/*.md text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/g1_proof/**/*.png binary
# Phase G Slice 4 proof tree is byte-compared by s4Parity, like the G1 tree.
/tools/s4_model_proofs.json text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/s4_proof/**/*.json text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/s4_proof/**/*.md text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/s4_proof/**/*.png binary
# The first Tier-2 slice's manifest and proof tree (2026-09-13; the T2a refuter, M1): the same rules as g1 / s4.
/tools/t2_model_proofs.json text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/t2_proof/**/*.json text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/t2_proof/**/*.md text eol=lf
/phase_g_reports/t2_proof/**/*.png binary
# Shipped GeckoLib rigs and clips are byte-compared against the proof copies by the asset audit (GECKO_GEO_PROOF_DRIFT); keep them LF on every checkout (2026-09-06).
/src/main/resources/assets/orespawn/geo/entity/*.geo.json text eol=lf
/src/main/resources/assets/orespawn/animations/entity/*.animation.json text eol=lf
# The asset audit is edited on every rig landing under core.autocrlf=true checkouts; keep it LF like the other tools (ENT-S-146 refuter B, D9, 2026-09-06).
/tools/asset_audit.py text eol=lf
# The keyframe reference leg's Beaver clip (tools/keyframe_clip.py output): the gametest resource is byte-equal to the SHIPPED clip the harness proves (item 15 landed 2026-09-12); LF (2026-09-06).
/src/gametest/resources/orespawn_gametest/keyframes/*.animation.json text eol=lf
# The clip generator and its per-species manifests are mirrored in the probe's in-memory twin and the clip is sha-pinned; keep them LF (item 15 refuter B, D9, 2026-09-06).
/tools/keyframe_clip.py text eol=lf
/tools/keyframe_clips/*.json text eol=lf
# The reference-only clips the sampler writes (ReferenceClipSampler, gradle referenceClips) and their index are sha-pinned by the package manifests and byte-compared between runs; keep them LF (owner 2026-09-13, second set, item 27 (3)).
/tools/reference_clips/*.json text eol=lf
